Feature: spa-cache-version
Target module: SPAEngine

- config.cacheVersion: a string or number naming the release the sessionStorage cache
  belongs to. Recorded under the sessionStorage key spaCacheVersion. When the configured
  value differs from the recorded one (or none is recorded), the engine empties its cache:
  at initialize() — before the entry route mounts — or immediately when set on a running
  engine. Same value = no-op. Non-empty string or finite number only (TypeError otherwise).
- clearCache(): resets linkContents, pageContents, pageSections and blockSections to empty
  objects, drops the no-web-storage fallback and the in-memory "already saved" trackers.
  Other sessionStorage keys (userProperties / auth) are untouched.
- Fix (exposed by clearing): the uncached branch of loadPageSections threw on a missing
  pageSections key (JSON.parse(undefined)), assigned an undeclared variable (ReferenceError
  in a module), fetched the section's config object instead of its .source URL, and never
  mounted the result. The cache builder had the same missing-key parse. All repaired.

Why: sessionStorage survives reloads, so after a deploy users with an open tab kept seeing
pre-deploy fragments with no way for the app to invalidate them short of closing the tab.

Verified: headless Chromium against examples/spa/server.py — boot clears a cache from a
different release and keeps one from the same release across reload; setting the same
version keeps the cache, a new one empties it and the next visit refetches; version.json
edited on disk is picked up by the Check button; clearCache() leaves the page's own key;
the empty-value validation error; uncached page section fetched, mounted and saved, and
refetched after clearCache(); the pre-change engine reproduced the page-section exception.
No page errors.

Affected projects: any consumer of vUX-spaEngine.js (app.myinvitees.com, vGet). No API
removed; behaviour is unchanged unless cacheVersion is set or clearCache() is called,
apart from the page-section fix.
